    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Daulton Varsho** (69.94) and **Taylor Ward** (67.66) stand as our elite plays, offering the highest efficiency scores against favorable matchups. **Daulton Varsho** benefits significantly from a high-upside matchup against Quantrill and a projected 100% stolen base opportunity due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s delivery cadence; combined with his spot in the 3-hole, he is our primary engine for power-speed production. Similarly, **Taylor Ward** thrives in today\u2019s environment; while he faces a decent arm in Griffin, the massive park factor boost (+16%) and his leadoff placement make him an essential start. **Tyler Freeman** (66.17) also merits attention as a strong play; his ability to exploit Paredes\u2019 high xERA (5.42) provides excellent value from the second base slot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Geraldo Perdomo** (47.91). While his spot in the 2-hole usually provides a floor, he narrowly missed the cut due to the overall depth of our middle infield and outfield configuration today. We are prioritizing the higher platoon and SP-skill advantages offered by **Bryson Stott** and **Masyn Winn**, whose matchups against Scott and Gusto respectively offer better statistical ceilings for run production. Meanwhile, **Jeremiah Jackson** (48.60) and **Drew Gilbert** (49.11) sit at the low end of our active starters; they are confirmed in the lineup, but their bottom-of-the-order positioning and unfavorable matchups against specific defensive setups keep their scores marginal.\n\nWe must remain cautious with **Jeremiah Jackson**, as he faces a challenging defensive situation\u2014specifically an elite opposing catcher\u2014which negatively impacts his stolen base potential despite the favorable park. Furthermore, **Yainer Diaz** and **Cal Raleigh** remain in the lineup despite scores under 60.00; while their efficiency is lower today, the scarcity of the catcher position and their specific platoon projections necessitate their inclusion. We continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** on the IL, as their absence remains a significant drag on our daily offensive ceiling.",
